+#       green. Vertical-travel instances therefore get horizontal yellow bands;
+#       horizontal-travel instances get vertical yellow bands.
+#   behavior_trace:
+#     - Base task, top-start example: the path descends until the first bar's
+#       forbidden halo blocks the next step, moves sideways along the unique
+#       closest safe row, then continues downward.
+#     - Variant: the same row is now colored yellow because every cell on that
+#       sideways run lies exactly one cell beyond the forbidden radius. The
+#       downward segments remain green.
+#     - Difference: the solver must not merely find a route; it must classify
+#       which routed cells belong to boundary-following detours.
+#   complexity_calibration:
+#     - We use one extra color only: yellow(4).
+#     - The mark repeats once per obstacle bar, so 2-4 examples are enough for
+#       a human to notice the consistent correspondence "one obstacle => one
+#       yellow detour segment".
+#     - We avoid more complicated per-bar color mappings or mixed marker types.
+#   implicit_assumptions_checked:
